License
-------
Apache License 2.0. The full license text is in the sibling LICENSE file.

Read this next paragraph before trusting the line above — the provenance here
is less direct than for models/ecapa/, and pretending otherwise would defeat
the point of writing it down.

The .task bundle itself carries NO embedded license: all four of its entries
were scanned for "Apache" / "licen" / "copyright" with zero hits, and the
TFLite metadata license field is unpopulated. The hosting bucket serves no
LICENSE file (HTTP 404 at three paths). The MediaPipe documentation licenses
only "the content of this page" and "code samples", not model weights. The
Apache-2.0 mediapipe wheel ships zero model files, and the Apache-2.0
google-ai-edge/mediapipe repository ships only .pbtxt graph configs for this
module -- no .tflite weights and no .task bundles at all.

The license is established instead from Google's own MODEL CARDS for the three
models this bundle repackages. Each of the three links to
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html:

  Model Card MediaPipe Face Mesh V2.pdf          -> face_landmarks_detector.tflite
  MediaPipe BlazeFace Model Card (Short Range).pdf -> face_detector.tflite
  Model Card Blendshape V2.pdf                   -> face_blendshapes.tflite

(all three under https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-assets/)

Those cards are image-only PDFs. A human read them on 2026-07-26 and reported
the Apache-2.0 license; that reading was then corroborated mechanically by
extracting each PDF's link annotations, which are plain objects even when the
page content is a flat image. What was machine-verified is the presence of the
Apache-2.0 URL in all three cards -- not the sentence surrounding it.

Full investigation, including the eight sources that said nothing:
  .harness/memory/research/2026-07-26-f5-face-landmarker-licence.md          (blocked)
  .harness/memory/research/2026-07-26-f5-face-landmarker-licence-resolved.md (resolved)

